A||||1||turbo86se||Can neon lights take the heat?||||1||
Z||000000||turbo86se||09-22-2001||11:53 AM||||As an experiment, while I've got the interior apart, I went ahead and wired a 15" neon light tube under the decklid. I mounted it just above where the recall strip goes. It's the only position where you can see anything through the scoop, and the vents. <BR>The neon light is not big enough, I need a 20" if made. <BR>My question is, do you think the neon light can take the heat under there and survive?<BR>TIA!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||09-22-2001||04:06 PM||||Depending on it's construction, the lamp should be ok. Hard to say really.<P>You'll want to get the balast out of there. That thing needs to be able to get rid of it's own heat and won't be able to do that well in a 200F engine bay.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/halfpole.gif"> <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
